sis in scope and exposes the complete conditional scalar-to-rooted construction. It is not a declaration that a minimizer exists.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-classical-fixed-minimizer"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","kind":"goal","label":"Conditional bounded synthesis input for a given minimizer","locator":"03-classical-optimization.tex:220–254, 553–608; eq:scalar-near-optimal-smooth and prop:classical-near-optimum","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","statement":"For every supplied admissible zero-temperature minimizer γ, every ε>0 and η_H>0, the same γ may be used to choose finite T,N,k, a bounded trigonometric formula and finite colors with one positive-probability helper type per propagation depth, total 0<p_H<η_H. The resulting m_col=Σ_c1_{C=c}sin(2θ_c) is centered, bounded by one, zero on helper roots, obeys all current/ancestor/helper exclusions and has E(m_col)≥P_*−ε. All choices are independent of D,n,J.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","id":"field:53f363240b407fdb2656a62d8b38a4d542ca0ee891a58931de316cf7f9d29618","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","id":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22c