risi functional; all later cutoff, mesh, smoothing, trigonometric and color choices are made for this gamma.","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment"},{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_admissible","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"The attaining gamma is a member of the same class U, so its admissibility is supplied with its minimality. Pure zero-field SK and the specified normalization remain the fixed domain of both statements. No SKSupport-to-SKValue model transport is asserted.","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment"}],"rationale":"The manuscript fixes an attained minimizer before constructing the bounded formula (the concluding construction is at lines 553–608). Applying the conditional construction to this common gamma supplies the closed existential input. The application is authored and remains subject to semantic review.","remaining_assumption_ids":[],"shared_bindings":{"gamma":"one minimizer gamma in the manuscript's zero-field pure-SK admissible class U, chosen by attainment and used throughout the fixed-minimizer construction"},"source_span":{"end_line":41,"source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","start_line":23},"status":"authored"},"application_metadata_scope":"remaining_assumption_ids is authored historical metadata, not an effective obligation audit; path-local suppression may be lifted for retained formal dependencies.","derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.classical_primary","id":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_primary%22%2C%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_primary%22%2C%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98